---
title: Match & Sort
description: Pair things up, then tip them into the right buckets. Two questions hide the targets entirely and make you type them from memory.
category: general knowledge
tags: [match, categorise, drag-and-drop]
:percent_to_win=60
:reveal_answers=after_every_question
:reveal_scores=after_every_question
:partial_credit=true
---

match: Match each invention to the person credited with it.
{
=The telephone -> Alexander Graham Bell
=The printing press -> Johannes Gutenberg
=The polio vaccine -> Jonas Salk
=Dynamite -> Alfred Nobel
}
:points_correct=2

match: Same idea, but the answers aren't on screen — type each one.
!<hint>[One for free (-1)](A hydrophone listens underwater.)
{
=Anemometer -> Wind speed
=Seismometer -> Earthquakes
=Hygrometer -> Humidity
}
:answer_mode=type
:typo_tolerance=30
:points_correct=2

categorise: Drop each animal into the group it belongs to.
!<analysis>[Why?](A bucket holds any number of items, which is what makes categorise different from match — several animals share "Mammal" here.)
{
=Dolphin -> Mammal
=Bat -> Mammal
=Ostrich -> Bird
=Penguin -> Bird
=Komodo dragon -> Reptile
}
:points_correct=1

categorise: Which country is each city in? Type it out.
{
=Osaka -> Japan
=Lyon -> France
=Porto -> Portugal
=Cusco -> Peru
}
:answer_mode=type
:match_case=false
:typo_tolerance=25
:points_correct=2
